00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:44.967
and it offers us an opportunity

00:02:44.967 --> 00:02:45.734
to reflect on the work we've

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.736
started and everything that we

00:02:47.736 --> 00:02:48.672
still want to achieve.

00:02:48.672 --> 00:02:51.675
We have made public safety the

00:02:51.675 --> 00:02:52.442
number one priority.

00:02:52.442 --> 00:02:54.842
Working relentlessly to provide

00:02:55.811 --> 00:02:56.512
clean and safe streets,

00:02:56.512 --> 00:02:58.912
confront the deadly fentanyl

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:00.683
crisis head on and connect

00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:01.217
people on the street to

00:03:01.217 --> 00:03:03.217
treatment and care.

00:03:04.287 --> 00:03:07.457
At the same time we are laying

00:03:07.457 --> 00:03:08.191
the groundwork to jumpstart our

00:03:08.191 --> 00:03:11.270
economy in our downtown core

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:11.728
along our commercial corridors

00:03:11.728 --> 00:03:14.128
and across our neighborhoods.

00:03:15.565 --> 00:03:18.401
I believe we're off to a strong

00:03:18.401 --> 00:03:19.103
start thanks in large part to

00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:19.569
the collaboration and support

00:03:19.569 --> 00:03:21.569
of this board.

00:03:22.906 --> 00:03:23.607
Together we pass the fentanyl

00:03:23.607 --> 00:03:26.700
state of emergency ordinance

00:03:26.776 --> 00:03:27.444
expedited legislation to unlock

00:03:27.444 --> 00:03:29.844
federal funds for critical

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.580
infrastructure and health

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.580
projects and advanced

00:03:34.417 --> 00:03:34.951
legislation to spur housing

00:03:34.951 --> 00:03:35.385
development in soma

00:03:35.385 --> 00:03:37.385
and downtown.

00:03:38.555 --> 00:03:41.458
We introduce new legislation to

00:03:41.458 --> 00:03:42.193
expand our entertainment zones

00:03:42.193 --> 00:03:42.826
and renew the first year free

00:03:42.826 --> 00:03:45.226
program to support small

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:46.764
businesses.

00:03:46.764 --> 00:03:49.400
And we announce two major

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.400
executive directives permit

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.139
S.F. And breaking the cycle.

00:03:56.139 --> 00:03:56.506
Property crime is down 35% from

00:03:56.506 --> 00:03:58.506
last year.

00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:01.309
Violent crime is down 15%

00:04:01.578 --> 00:04:01.946
and car break ins are at 22

00:04:01.946 --> 00:04:03.946
year lows.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:08.418
Muni ridership is back at 75%

00:04:08.418 --> 00:04:11.418
of 2019 levels and for the

00:04:12.189 --> 00:04:12.956
first time in years people feel

00:04:12.956 --> 00:04:16.930
san francisco is headed in the

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:16.894
right direction.

00:04:16.894 --> 00:04:20.131
So much of the progress we've

00:04:20.131 --> 00:04:20.932
made as a city stems from a

00:04:20.932 --> 00:04:21.232
major change right here at city

00:04:21.232 --> 00:04:23.232
hall.

00:04:24.101 --> 00:04:24.402
The new era of collaboration is

00:04:24.402 --> 00:04:26.402
real.

00:04:27.438 --> 00:04:27.838
We prove it to san franciscans

00:04:27.838 --> 00:04:29.838
every day.

00:04:30.974 --> 00:04:31.942
When you call me about a

00:04:31.942 --> 00:04:34.546
